# Responsive Design

- Support desktop, laptop, tablet, and mobile.
- Prefer responsive CSS over duplicated markup; avoid separate desktop/mobile implementations unless necessary.
- Use design references as breakpoint/layout source of truth.
- Preserve spacing and hierarchy across breakpoints.
- Avoid arbitrary breakpoint proliferation.
- Verify important responsive states before calling work complete.
